.\" Manpage for SandboxAuditor
.TH SANDBOXAUDITOR 1 "October 2026" "v1.0.0" "SandboxAuditor Manual"
.SH NAME
SandboxAuditor \- Restricted user sandbox orchestration and privilege audit suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo SandboxAuditor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIUSERNAME\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SandboxAuditor
is a security utility for Linux systems designed to provision restricted user environments (\fBrbash\fR), enforce strict filesystem masks, and perform privilege exposure audits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B <username>
Default positional action. Audits the specified user's home directory tree for permission drift and exposed sensitive keys.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-audit " \fIUSERNAME\fR"
Explicitly executes a privilege and file exposure audit on \fIUSERNAME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Scans the system account database (\fI/etc/passwd\fR) and lists all active accounts configured with the restricted shell (\fI/bin/rbash\fR).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-create " \fIUSERNAME\fR"
Provisions a new restricted sandbox user, configuring \fIrbash\fR, applying a strict \fBumask 027\fR setting, and locking down home directory ownership to root (\fB750\fR).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delete " \fIUSERNAME\fR"
Tears down an existing sandbox account and purges the associated home directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays the command-line help menu and exits.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Provision a new sandbox user:
.B sudo SandboxAuditor --create testuser
.TP
List active sandbox accounts:
.B sudo SandboxAuditor --list
.TP
Audit a user's home directory:
.B sudo SandboxAuditor testuser
.TP
Delete a sandbox user:
.B sudo SandboxAuditor --delete testuser
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (missing arguments, missing root privileges, or execution error).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rbash (1),
.BR chmod (1),
.BR umask (2)